QEMU 11.0.0 aborts in hvf_arch_init_vcpu on macOS 15.2+ (incl. Tahoe):
a g_assert checks that Apple's HV_SYS_REG_SMCR_EL1 enum equals QEMU's
KVMID-derived encoding, which does not hold for the SME registers in the
current Apple SDK. SME2/HVF support is still in-flight upstream. The
linux-builder guest is plain Linux and never touches SME, so drop the
sanity assert to let the VM boot.

--- a/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c
+++ b/target/arm/hvf/hvf.c
@@ -1259,8 +1259,7 @@
             sregs_match_len += ARRAY_SIZE(hvf_sreg_list_sme2) + 1;
         }

-#define DEF_SYSREG_15_02(HVF_ID, ...) \
-        g_assert(HVF_ID == KVMID_TO_HVF(KVMID_AA64_SYS_REG64(__VA_ARGS__)));
+#define DEF_SYSREG_15_02(HVF_ID, ...)
 #define DEF_SYSREG(...)

 #include "sysreg.c.inc"
